@NODE INTRO "Introduction..."

RTW (Real Time Who) from the Myth /X )-Sign Development team is a small,
fast and no-nonsense replacement door for the built-in 'WHO' command in
AmiExpress. With this door it is possible to spy on all the other nodes in
real time, so there is no need to type WHO every second to see the actions
of the other users who are logged on your bulletin board system.
RTW requires OS2.04 (V37) and AmiExpress V3.xx or higher.

    @{"BACK TO MAIN" link "Main" 0}
@ENDNODE

@NODE INSTALL "Installation..."

To install RTW, just copy ALL files in the RTW/BBS drawer to your BBS:
directory, that means that you need the logical assignment BBS:
BBS: is an assignment to the root directory of AmiExpress. (configured in
the ACP.info, for example, BBS_LOCATION=BBS:) Further you need the logical
assignment DOORS: (DOORS: is an assignment to your BBS:Doors directory).


TOOLTYPES IN BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/WHO.info
-----------------------------------------

============== CUT HERE =============
LOCATION=BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/RTW     - Specifies the location of the door
MULTINODE=YES                        - tells /X if the module may be
                                       simultaneously accessed from other
                                       nodes.
ACCESS=10                            - tells /X the access level required
                                       to run this door.
TYPE=XIM                             - RTW is a XIM door.
STACK=4096                           - Specifies the stack needed to
                                       launch the door.
============== CUT HERE =============

If you have done all this then you have installed Real Time Who correctly,
congratulations!

    @{"BACK TO MAIN" link "Main" 0}
@ENDNODE

@NODE USAGE "Usage..."

Usage is simple, by typing 'WHO' you can actually launch the door. The
following text (for example) is displayed on screen:

  Nd   Name                Location           Action            Misc Info
.----+-------------------+------------------+-----------------+--------------.
| 00 | Your Node         |                  | uSING rTW v2.00 |              |
| 01 | cREW^oNE          | -*- M Y T H -*-  | uPLOADING       | MTH-RTW2.LHA |
| 02 | eUROSOFT          | -*- M Y T H -*-  | iRC-CHAT-bOX    |              |
| 03 | pLL               | -*- M Y T H -*-  | iRC-cHAT-bOX    |              |
| 04 | dIABLO            | -*- M Y T H -*-  | iRC-cHAT-bOXL   |              |
| 05 | dELITE            | -*- M Y T H -*-  | dOWNLOADING     | MTH-RTW2.LHA |
| 06 | .oO NOBODY Oo.    | .oO NOWHERE Oo.  | aWAITING cALL   |              |
|____|___________________|__________________|_________________|______________|
 |___________ _____ ____ ___ ___ __ _            rTW v2.00 bY cREW^oNE!mYTH  |
                                      - -- --- ---- -------------------------'

    @{"BACK TO MAIN" link "Main" 0}
@ENDNODE

@NODE VERSION "Revision History..."

 V1.0 - 09 Jun 1995
      - First public release
 V2.0 - 24 Jun 1995
      - Now using multicom semaphores

If you have any suggestions, bug reports or questions, please contact Crew
One at one of the electronic mail addresses.

When sending in bug reports, please state exactly under what circumstances
the bug occurred, what equipment was used and what happened. If possible
also try to give me enough information to reproduce the bug. It is very
difficult to find bugs when you don't know exactly what happened. Please
don't just send messages like "RTW doesn't work", that really doesn't help
me. If possible, submit the offending 'error' to me so I can test it myself,
or give me a pointer where I can find the error.

    @{"BACK TO MAIN" link "Main" 0}
@ENDNODE

